---
/**
 * The SMART Studio minisite (/studio): viewing and authoring SMART
 * Recommendations — the canvas where an expert models a Recommendation
 * and the model is the published artifact. Style: the OIML SMART writing
 * guide.
 */
const capabilities = [
  { name: 'The model canvas', desc: 'A Recommendation is authored as a graph: subjects, attributes, processes, and mappings, drawn and connected directly.' },
  { name: 'Inspectors', desc: 'Every node carries its properties, constraints, and provenance in a structured inspector, validated as it is edited.' },
  { name: 'The document map', desc: 'Each model element cites its clause in the source publication, so the model reads against the document line by line.' },
  { name: 'Validation', desc: 'The package is checked as it is built: schema, semantics, and the drift guards that keep a published model honest.' },
]
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>SMART Studio — OIML SMART</title>
    <meta name="description" content="OIML SMART Studio — the tool for viewing and authoring SMART Recommendations." />
    <style>
      :root {
        --paper: #faf7f2; --ink: #1a2332; --ink-soft: #4a5568; --accent: #004996;
        --rule: #d9d4c7; --paper-soft: #f3efe7;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --paper: #14181f; --ink: #e8e6e1; --ink-soft: #a8b0bc; --accent: #6ba3e8; --rule: #2c3542; --paper-soft: #1c222c; }
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; line-height: 1.6; }
      main { max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem; }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.025em; line-height: 1.05; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem; }
      h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
      p { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 42rem; }
      .lede { font-size: 1.125rem; }
      .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
      .brand:hover { color: var(--accent); }
      ul { color: var(--ink-soft); }
      li { margin: 0.375rem 0; }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
      footer { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a class="brand" href="https://www.oimlsmart.org/">← OIML SMART</a>
      <picture>
        <source srcset="https://www.oimlsmart.org/img/components/smart-studio-dark.svg" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
        <img src="https://www.oimlsmart.org/img/components/smart-studio-light.svg" alt="The SMART Studio logo." width="140" />
      </picture>
      <h1>SMART Studio</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        SMART Studio is the tool for viewing and authoring SMART Recommendations. An expert models a
        Recommendation on a canvas of subjects, processes, and mappings, and the model itself is the
        published artifact: versioned, validated, and citable back to the source document.
      </p>

      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        A SMART Recommendation begins as an expert reading of a published OIML Recommendation. The
        Studio is where that reading becomes a model: the requirements, tests, and forms are drawn as
        a structured graph, each element carrying its provenance. The Studio removes the gap between
        the document and the machine-readable form, because the model the expert draws is the model
        the program publishes.
      </p>

      <h2>What the Studio provides</h2>
      <ul>
        {capabilities.map(c => (
          <li><strong>{c.name}.</strong> {c.desc}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Lineage</h2>
      <p>
        The Studio descends from the MMEL editor built for the first SMART-document pilots, rebuilt on
        the Primmel language and the current platform. The editing model is unchanged: graphical
        construction of the subject, its aspects, its processes, and the mappings between reference
        and implementation models. The current Studio adds validation, packaging, and the direct hand
        off to the OIML-CS SMART platform.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the Studio sits</h2>
      <p>
        The Studio is the authoring half of the toolchain. The OIML-CS SMART platform is the running
        half: what an expert authors in the Studio, the platform renders, tests, and certifies. The
        Studio is developed as part of the Primmel platform, and the OIML SMART program builds its
        Recommendation authoring practice on it.
      </p>

      <footer>
        Part of <a href="https://www.oimlsmart.org/">OIML SMART</a>. Developed under the OIML SMART program by Ribose.
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
